  "description": "EXADEO crystallizes in the cubic crystal system with space group I -4 3 d. Reported CIF formula moiety: C88 H116 Gd4 N12 Ni4 O24 4+,4(C1 H4 O1),25.3(H2 O1),4(Cl1 1-). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Ni1 (Ni) has 3 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Ni2 (Ni) has 3 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Ni3 (Ni) has 3 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Ni4 (Ni) has 3 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.232-4.269 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 84.91-139.76°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Gd4Ni4(H3L)4(μ3-OH)4(μ2-OH)4]Cl4·25.3H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 μ2-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 μ2-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
